# Expo/React Native resolve packages by walking node_modules up from the
# project root, so they need their transitive deps visible at the workspace
# root. pnpm's default isolated linker hides them, which broke every mobile
# release: the Android build failed in :app:createBundleReleaseJsAndAssets,
# first on "The required package `expo-asset` cannot be found", then on
# "Cannot find module 'babel-preset-expo'" — both transitives of expo.
#
# Expo documents node-linker=hoisted for pnpm monorepos, but that fails on
# this workspace: pnpm aborts with "Invalid Version:" while deduplicating
# bins across all packages. Hoisting only the mobile toolchain gets the same
# resolution without touching the layout every other app builds against.
public-hoist-pattern[]=*expo*
public-hoist-pattern[]=metro*
public-hoist-pattern[]=@react-native/*
public-hoist-pattern[]=react-native*
public-hoist-pattern[]=@babel/*
public-hoist-pattern[]=babel-*
public-hoist-pattern[]=hermes-*
